---
/**
 * Edicion — shared body of `/ediciones/[slug]` and `/en/editions/[slug]`
 * (SM-040, SM-041, SM-048).
 *
 * The two routes are the same page in two languages, so the whole body lives
 * here and each route file under `src/pages/` is a thin wrapper that keeps its
 * own `getStaticPaths`, resolves the entry and fixes `idioma` (skill
 * `paginas-bilingues`, "La gemela EN es el mismo archivo con `idioma = 'en'`").
 * Nothing below changed with the move except the locale, which arrives as a
 * prop instead of being hardcoded and is now passed explicitly to `Pagina`
 * rather than left to `Astro.currentLocale`, and the markdown body (see the
 * OBSERVACIÓN at the end of this header).
 *
 * `/ediciones/[slug]` — the page that reproduces the edition poster on the web
 * (SM-040; sitemap.md §2.6, design-system.md §8, empty gallery §3.4). Built
 * against `design/Edicion.dc.html` ("Edición 01 · Desktop" and "· Mobile"),
 * which is the approved design and therefore wins over sitemap.md wherever the
 * two disagree — every divergence is reported below, none is resolved
 * unilaterally (CLAUDE.md).
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (bloque 3, `SelloHorario`): sitemap.md §2.6 lists a `SelloHorario`
 * under the headline. The lamina has none, and says so in its own NOTA PARA
 * DESARROLLO ("Sin SelloHorario en esta página (los horarios ya están en el
 * BloqueFicha)"), matching diseno-web-indice.md decision 10 and the note at the
 * end of `SelloHorario.astro` itself. Not rendered. The entry's `selloHorario`
 * field stays unused by this page.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (bloque 2, slot del titular): sitemap.md §2.6 puts the `claim` as
 * an `Anotacion` in the slot with a `Sello` overlaid. The lamina puts the
 * `Escudo` in the slot and `marca/subtitulo-experiencia.png` under the headline,
 * with no `Sello` and no claim anywhere on the page. The lamina is followed;
 * `claim[idioma]` still ships as the page's meta description (and as the JSON-LD
 * `description` in SM-041), so the data is not dropped, only placed where the
 * design puts it.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (bloque 2, tamaño del titular): the lamina sets `TitularPartido`
 * at 11rem desktop / 3rem mobile, and diseno-web-indice.md repeats it ("el
 * TitularPartido de la edición en 11rem"). The component only offers `xl`
 * (`clamp(4.5rem, 16vw, 14rem)`) and `lg`, neither of which is that curve, and
 * it takes no size prop. `--text-display-xl` is scoped on the wrapper instead —
 * the same custom-property idiom `FichaFotografo.astro` already uses for
 * `--text-manuscrita` — so no component and no token file is touched.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (bloque 4, descripción): the lamina replaces the description with
 * a "Cómo funcionó" list of three numbered steps ("Aporte solidario al
 * llegar.", "Recorrido por los sets 001 a 007.", "Las fotos llegan por
 * email."). Those three lines exist nowhere in the content model, while
 * `descripcion[idioma]` — which says the same thing in one paragraph — does. The
 * lamina's section heading is kept and filled with the real field rather than
 * re-typing the design's paraphrase into the dictionaries as if it were
 * content.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (bloque 5, FOTEAN): sitemap.md §2.6 and this ticket ask for an
 * `Aparejo` of `CajaNombre`. The lamina uses `FichaFotografo` in a 4-column
 * grid (1 on mobile) — the component exists, is built for exactly this section,
 * and links the whole card to the profile, so the acceptance criterion ("las
 * cajas de FOTEAN y EXPONEN linkean a los perfiles") holds either way. The
 * lamina is followed. An artist with no `obra` cannot fill a `FichaFotografo`
 * (its `obraPrincipal` is required), so that case degrades to a linked
 * `CajaNombre` instead of an empty card; nobody in edición 01 hits it today.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (bloque 5, qué foto): the lamina's card for Herick Frontado uses
 * `herick-frontado-02.png` while every other card uses its artist's first work.
 * Nothing in the `artistas` schema marks a "card" image, so `obra[0]` is used
 * for everyone — Herick's card shows `01.png` instead of `02.png`.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (bloque 7, MÚSICA): sitemap.md §2.6 describes a mono
 * `ETIQUETA:`/valores block. The lamina uses one `CajaNombre` per act, which is
 * what this page renders, with the Instagram profile as its `href` when the
 * handle is not a placeholder (MAVAREZ's `[HANDLE MAVAREZ]` renders as plain
 * text, no link — CLAUDE.md, "un dato inventado es un error grave"). The
 * lamina's mobile screen passes `chica` to those boxes (32px tall); they are
 * links, so the normal 44px size is kept at every width (design-system.md §12,
 * "objetivo táctil ≥ 44 px").
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (bloque 9, la jornada): the lamina's collage is ten works from
 * `assets/obra/` laid over 12 columns. The `galeria` field of this edition holds
 * the three photos of the day (`pusadolfo-01`, `sin-atribuir-*`), which this
 * ticket's non-negotiable rules confine to exactly this block — so the collage
 * renders `galeria`, cycling the lamina's first three positions and rotations.
 * `FotoPegada` has no `pie` prop (the lamina's does), so each `credito` is
 * printed under its photo by this page, in `grafito`, as the ticket asks.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (bloque 9, PalabrasClave): the lamina places the vertical mark at
 * `right: -88px`, outside its 1280px container. At a 1280px-wide viewport the
 * container has no side margin left, so any negative offset would produce a
 * horizontal scrollbar (an explicit acceptance criterion of this ticket). It is
 * pinned to the container's right edge instead, inside its 48px padding.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (bloque 11, cierre): sitemap.md §2.6 closes with an `Anotacion`
 * reading "Unidos por la reconstrucción" plus the `Boton` sello "Cómo apoyar".
 * That phrase appears nowhere in the lamina, in the design system or in the
 * content, so it is not written: the closing section ships the `Boton` alone.
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (cuerpo markdown): the lamina has no block for the entry's
 * markdown body. It is rendered under "Cómo funcionó", after
 * `descripcion[idioma]`, as the section that already tells how the edition
 * worked. It carries the visible placeholder "[CIFRAS DE LA EDICIÓN 01: …]" — a
 * placeholder, never a figure (this ticket: "sin cifras de recaudación en
 * ninguna página").
 *
 * OBSERVACIÓN (cuerpo markdown en inglés, SM-048): the content model has no
 * English version of that body — the `ediciones` schema types every public text
 * as `{ es, en }` except the markdown, which `glob` + `render()` keep
 * single-language. So `<Content />` renders on the Spanish route only, and the
 * English one shows `comun.cuerpoEnPendiente` ("[BODY EN PENDING]") in its
 * place: a visible placeholder, never untranslated Spanish inside an English
 * page (CLAUDE.md, "Bilingüe siempre"). The fix belongs in
 * `modelo-de-contenido.md` — one body per language, e.g. `cuerpo/<slug>.es.md`
 * + `.en.md` or a `cuerpoEn` field — and `src/content.config.ts` is outside
 * this ticket's Alcance.
 */
import { getEntries, render } from 'astro:content';
import type { CollectionEntry } from 'astro:content';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import Anotacion from '../../Anotacion.astro';
import BloqueFicha from '../../BloqueFicha.astro';
import Boton from '../../Boton.astro';
import CajaNombre from '../../CajaNombre.astro';
import Escudo from '../../Escudo.astro';
import FichaFotografo from '../../FichaFotografo.astro';
import FotoPegada from '../../FotoPegada.astro';
import FranjaAliados from '../../FranjaAliados.astro';
import PalabrasClave from '../../PalabrasClave.astro';
import TitularPartido from '../../TitularPartido.astro';
import Aparejo from '../Aparejo.astro';
import Lightbox from '../Lightbox.astro';
import CuerpoEnPendiente from './CuerpoEnPendiente.astro';
import Pagina from '../../../layouts/Pagina.astro';
import escudoImagen from '../../../assets/marca/escudo.png';
import palabrasClaveImagen from '../../../assets/marca/palabras-clave.png';
import subtituloExperiencia from '../../../assets/marca/subtitulo-experiencia.png';
import manuscritaFotografos from '../../../assets/manuscritas/marca/fotografos.png';
import manuscritaExponen from '../../../assets/manuscritas/marca/exponen.png';
import {
  direccionSinCiudad,
  esPlaceholder,
  etiquetaCortaDeEdicion,
  fechaCorta,
  fechaHoraIso,
  rangoDeSets,
  retratoTamano,
  urlDeInstagram,
} from '../ediciones.ts';
import { rutaLocalizada, t, type Idioma } from '../../../i18n/utils.ts';

interface Props {
  /** Locale of the route rendering this body; each wrapper fixes it literally. */
  idioma: Idioma;
  /** Entry resolved by the wrapper's own `getStaticPaths`. */
  edicion: CollectionEntry<'ediciones'>;
}

const { idioma, edicion } = Astro.props;
const { data } = edicion;

const { Content } = await render(edicion);

/**
 * Body of the "Cómo funcionó" section: the entry's markdown on the Spanish
 * route, the `[BODY EN PENDING]` placeholder on the English one. A dynamic tag
 * (`<Cuerpo />`) rather than a conditional inside the wrapper, so the Spanish
 * markup — and with it the built HTML, whitespace included — is byte for byte
 * the one this page shipped before the two routes started sharing a body.
 */
const Cuerpo = idioma === 'es' ? Content : CuerpoEnPendiente;

const fotean = await getEntries(data.fotean);
const exponen = await getEntries(data.exponen);
const aliados = await getEntries(data.aliados);

const etiquetaCorta = etiquetaCortaDeEdicion(data.nombre);

const lugar = {
  nombre: data.lugar.nombre,
  direccion: direccionSinCiudad(data.lugar.direccion, data.ciudad),
  ciudad: `${data.ciudad}, ${data.pais}`,
};

/**
 * "Seres" / "Migratorios" for `TitularPartido`, split off the brand name in the
 * dictionaries instead of being typed here: CLAUDE.md never translates it, and
 * `seo.tituloSitio` is where it already lives.
 */
const marca = t(idioma, 'seo.tituloSitio');
const espacio = marca.indexOf(' ');
const tituloArriba = espacio === -1 ? marca : marca.slice(0, espacio);
const tituloAbajo = espacio === -1 ? '' : marca.slice(espacio + 1);

/** Local stand-in for `t()`'s missing interpolation — same helper as `Sello.astro`. */
function interpolar(plantilla: string, valores: Record<string, string>): string {
  return Object.entries(valores).reduce(
    (acumulado, [clave, valor]) => acumulado.replaceAll(`{${clave}}`, valor),
    plantilla
  );
}

// "Fotean · Sets 001 – 007" (Edicion.dc.html). Without a single `numero` among
// them the range is dropped rather than invented.
const sets = rangoDeSets(fotean.map((artista) => artista.data.numero));
const leyendaFotean =
  sets === null
    ? t(idioma, 'ediciones.fotean')
    : interpolar(t(idioma, 'ediciones.foteanSets'), sets);

const leyendaExponen = interpolar(t(idioma, 'ediciones.exposicion'), { edicion: etiquetaCorta });

const itemsExponen = exponen.map((artista) => ({
  texto: artista.data.nombre,
  href: rutaLocalizada(`/artistas/${artista.data.slug}`, idioma),
}));

/**
 * The collage of `design/Edicion.dc.html`, "LA JORNADA": on desktop, the
 * lamina's first three 12-column slots and their vertical offsets, cycled;
 * on mobile, its alternating 88% / 80% widths and sides. Class strings are
 * literal because Tailwind's scanner reads source text, never a computed name.
 * Placement lives on this wrapper, not on `FotoPegada` (decision 13).
 *
 * `grid` on the wrapper is load-bearing, not decoration. `.foto-pegada`
 * (theme.css) is `inline-block`, so with `width: auto` it shrinks to fit its
 * content — and its `<img>` is `w-full`, i.e. a percentage of that same
 * shrink-to-fit width. The circular reference resolves to the image's intrinsic
 * width (244px for `sin-atribuir-puente`, and 0 before a `loading="lazy"` image
 * has decoded), never to the column. As a grid item the box blockifies and
 * `justify-self: stretch` gives it the definite width the percentage needs, which
 * is exactly what the lamina passes its own FotoPegada as `ancho="100%"`.
 *
 * Each slot is additionally capped at its photo's own natural width with an
 * inline `max-width` (geometry inline, colors as tokens — the split
 * `FranjaAliados.astro` and `HiloTricolor.astro` already use). The three photos
 * of the day are 578, 244 and 268px wide: without the cap the two portraits
 * would be blown up to a 586px column, and since all three are roughly the same
 * height (386 / 366 / 378px), capping by width also lands them at the
 * near-equal heights the lamina's slots have (420 / 380 / 320px) without
 * cropping anything.
 */
const POSICIONES = [
  'grid w-[88%] self-start md:col-span-6 md:col-start-1 md:w-auto',
  'grid w-[80%] self-end md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7 md:mt-40 md:w-auto',
  'grid w-[80%] self-start md:col-span-4 md:col-start-2 md:mt-10 md:w-auto',
];

/** design-system.md §7 item 7 keeps every tilt inside [-2, 2]. */
const ROTACIONES = [-2, 1.5, -1];

/**
 * The same photos, in the shape `internos/Lightbox.astro` takes (SM-038). The
 * collage keeps the lamina's own slots instead of `Galeria.astro`'s artist
 * layout; the viewer only needs each anchor to carry `data-galeria-foto` +
 * `data-indice`, which is what it binds to. The credit doubles as the
 * caption's title ("Edición 01 · [AUTORÍA A CONFIRMAR]").
 */
const fotosDelDia = data.galeria.map((foto) => ({
  imagen: foto.image,
  alt: foto.alt[idioma],
  titulo: foto.credito,
}));

/**
 * One chip per act (Edicion.dc.html "MÚSICA"), linked to its Instagram profile
 * only when the handle is a real one: MAVAREZ's `[HANDLE MAVAREZ]` is a valid
 * placeholder but never a usable URL (CLAUDE.md, "un dato inventado es un error
 * grave").
 */
const itemsMusica = data.musica.map((acto) => {
  const handle = acto.instagram;
  return {
    texto: acto.nombre,
    href: handle === undefined || esPlaceholder(handle) ? undefined : urlDeInstagram(handle),
  };
});

const rutaEdiciones = rutaLocalizada('/ediciones', idioma);

/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   JSON-LD Event (SM-041)

   OBSERVACIÓN (dónde va): the ticket asks for the `<script>` in the `<head>`.
   Neither `Pagina.astro` nor `Base.astro` exposes a `head` slot, and both are
   outside this ticket's Alcance, so it is emitted as the first node of the
   page's content instead. Google reads structured data from anywhere in the
   document ("Structured data general guidelines": the markup may be in the
   `<head>` or the `<body>`), so this stays valid; when a `head` slot lands, the
   block moves without any change to the object below.

   OBSERVACIÓN (`eventStatus`): schema.org's `EventStatusType` enumerates
   Scheduled / Cancelled / Postponed / Rescheduled / MovedOnline — there is no
   value for "already happened". A `pasada` edition therefore keeps
   `EventScheduled`, which is what it was: the property describes whether the
   event runs as announced, not whether it is over. `estado` still selects it
   explicitly so a future `proxima`/cancelled distinction has one place to live.

   SM-048: the object is emitted in the language of the page it belongs to.
   `description` reads `claim[idioma]` and `url` is that page's own canonical
   URL, so the English twin advertises `/en/editions/<slug>/` with the English
   claim. `name` is the edition's real `nombre` and `organizer.name` the brand:
   both proper names, identical in either language (CLAUDE.md, "No se
   traducen"). Nothing beyond the ticket's list is emitted: no `inLanguage`, no
   `offers`, no price, no attendance figures.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

interface LugarJsonLd {
  '@type': 'Place';
  name: string;
  address: string;
}

interface PersonaJsonLd {
  '@type': 'Person';
  name: string;
}

interface OrganizacionJsonLd {
  '@type': 'Organization';
  name: string;
  url: string;
}

interface EventoJsonLd {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org';
  '@type': 'Event';
  name: string;
  description: string;
  startDate: string;
  endDate: string;
  eventStatus: string;
  location: LugarJsonLd;
  organizer: OrganizacionJsonLd;
  performer: PersonaJsonLd[];
  url: string;
  image?: string;
}

/** `site` of astro.config.mjs; the page's own origin is only a build-time guard. */
const base = Astro.site ?? new URL(Astro.url.origin);
const urlCanonica = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, base).href;

const evento: EventoJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Event',
  name: data.nombre,
  description: data.claim[idioma],
  startDate: fechaHoraIso(data.fecha, data.horario.desde),
  endDate: fechaHoraIso(data.fecha, data.horario.hasta),
  eventStatus: 'https://schema.org/EventScheduled',
  location: {
    '@type': 'Place',
    name: data.lugar.nombre,
    address: `${lugar.direccion}, ${data.ciudad}, ${data.pais}`,
  },
  organizer: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: marca,
    url: base.href,
  },
  performer: [
    ...fotean.map((artista) => artista.data.nombre),
    ...data.musica.map((a) => a.nombre),
  ].map((nombre) => ({ '@type': 'Person', name: nombre }) satisfies PersonaJsonLd),
  url: urlCanonica,
  ...(data.imagenOg === undefined ? {} : { image: new URL(data.imagenOg.src, base).href }),
};

/**
 * `<` is escaped so no content value can ever close the `<script>` element
 * early (HTML spec, "restrictions for contents of script elements"); `\u003c`
 * is still the same string to any JSON parser.
 */
const eventoJson = JSON.stringify(evento).replaceAll('<', '\\u003c');
---

<Pagina
  titulo={data.nombre}
  descripcion={data.claim[idioma]}
  imagenOg={data.imagenOg}
  idioma={idioma}
  rutaActual={Astro.url.pathname}
  contenedor={false}
>
  {/* JSON-LD Event (SM-041) — see the OBSERVACIÓN about placement above. */}
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={eventoJson} />

  {/* FICHA DE LA EDICIÓN (Edicion.dc.html:36) */}
  <section class="contenedor flex flex-col items-start gap-6 pt-6 md:gap-8 md:pt-12">
    <a
      href={rutaEdiciones}
      class="font-mono text-etiqueta text-azul-sello inline-block py-3 font-bold uppercase underline underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors duration-150 hover:text-azul-marcador focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-azul-sello"
      >{t(idioma, 'ediciones.volver')}</a
    >
    <div class="relative w-full">
      <BloqueFicha
        fecha={fechaCorta(data.fecha)}
        horario={data.horario.etiqueta}
        lugar={lugar}
        idioma={idioma}
      />
      {
        /* The lamina's -4° is outside `Anotacion`'s [-3, 2] range and would be
          clamped anyway; -3° is passed explicitly. `--text-manuscrita` carries the
          lamina's 1.5rem mobile / 1.75rem desktop size onto the component's own
          `text-manuscrita` utility. */
      }
      <div
        class="absolute right-0 -top-1 whitespace-nowrap [--text-manuscrita:1.5rem] md:-top-14 md:[--text-manuscrita:1.75rem]"
      >
        <Anotacion texto={etiquetaCorta} rotacion={-3} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* TITULAR (Edicion.dc.html:44) — the page's single <h1> */}
  <section class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 pt-8 pb-12 md:gap-8 md:pt-12 md:pb-20">
    <div class="contenedor [--text-display-xl:clamp(3rem,12vw,11rem)]">
      <TitularPartido arriba={tituloArriba} abajo={tituloAbajo}>
        <div class="w-[146px] md:w-[259px]">
          <Escudo imagen={escudoImagen} ancho={259} />
        </div>
      </TitularPartido>
    </div>
    <div class="w-[260px] max-w-full md:w-[520px]">
      <Image
        src={subtituloExperiencia}
        alt={t(idioma, 'ediciones.subtituloExperienciaAlt')}
        widths={[260, 520, subtituloExperiencia.width]}
        sizes="(min-width: 768px) 520px, 260px"
        loading="lazy"
        class="block h-auto w-full"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* CÓMO FUNCIONÓ (Edicion.dc.html:57) */}
  <section class="contenedor seccion grilla-4-8">
    <h2 class="seccion-titulo">{t(idioma, 'ediciones.comoFunciono')}</h2>
    <div class="flex max-w-[65ch] flex-col gap-4 font-mono text-base leading-relaxed text-pretty">
      <p class="text-tinta m-0">{data.descripcion[idioma]}</p>
      {
        /* The entry's markdown body. Its paragraphs are direct children of this
          flex column, so `gap-4` spaces them without a prose plugin. On the
          English route the body has no translation in the content model, so the
          slot carries the `[BODY EN PENDING]` placeholder instead (SM-048; see
          the OBSERVACIÓN in this file's header). */
      }
      <div class="text-tinta-suave flex flex-col gap-4"><Cuerpo /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* FOTEAN (Edicion.dc.html:82) */}
  <section class="contenedor seccion flex flex-col gap-8 md:gap-12">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between md:gap-6">
      <div class="w-[300px] max-w-full md:w-[420px]">
        <Anotacion
          imagen={manuscritaFotografos}
          alt={t(idioma, 'ediciones.anotacionFotean')}
          rotacion={-2}
          ancho={420}
        />
      </div>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-etiqueta text-grafito m-0 font-bold uppercase">{leyendaFotean}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 md:grid-cols-4 md:gap-x-8 md:gap-y-12">
      {
        fotean.map((artista) => {
          const perfil = rutaLocalizada(`/artistas/${artista.data.slug}`, idioma);
          const [obra] = artista.data.obra;
          if (obra === undefined) {
            // No work uploaded yet: `FichaFotografo` requires `obraPrincipal`,
            // so the name alone links to the profile instead of an empty card.
            return <CajaNombre texto={artista.data.nombre} href={perfil} />;
          }
          return (
            <FichaFotografo
              numero={artista.data.numero}
              nombre={artista.data.nombre}
              obraPrincipal={obra.image}
              obraAlt={obra.alt[idioma]}
              retrato={artista.data.retrato}
              retratoAlt={artista.data.retratoAlt[idioma]}
              retratoTamano={
                artista.data.retrato
                  ? retratoTamano(artista.data.retrato.width, artista.data.retrato.height)
                  : undefined
              }
              instagram={artista.data.instagram}
              href={perfil}
              idioma={idioma}
            />
          );
        })
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* EXPONEN (Edicion.dc.html:96) */}
  <section class="contenedor seccion flex flex-col items-center gap-8 md:gap-12">
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-3">
      <div class="w-[240px] max-w-full md:w-[320px]">
        <Anotacion
          imagen={manuscritaExponen}
          alt={t(idioma, 'ediciones.anotacionExponen')}
          rotacion={-2}
          ancho={320}
        />
      </div>
      <h2 class="font-mono text-etiqueta text-grafito m-0 font-bold uppercase">{leyendaExponen}</h2>
    </div>
    <Aparejo items={itemsExponen} filas={[3, 3, 3]} filasMobile={[2, 1]} />
  </section>

  {/* MÚSICA (Edicion.dc.html:105) */}
  <section class="contenedor seccion grilla-4-8">
    <h2 class="seccion-titulo">{t(idioma, 'ficha.musica')}</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 md:gap-4">
      {itemsMusica.map((acto) => <CajaNombre texto={acto.texto} href={acto.href} />)}
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ALIADOS (Edicion.dc.html:117) */}
  <section class="contenedor seccion grilla-4-8 md:items-center">
    <h2 class="seccion-titulo">{t(idioma, 'ediciones.aliados')}</h2>
    <FranjaAliados
      aliados={aliados}
      altoLogo={48}
      altoLogoMobile={48}
      separacion={48}
      separacionMobile={48}
      justificar="inicio"
      idioma={idioma}
    />
  </section>

  {/* LA JORNADA (Edicion.dc.html:123) */}
  <section class="contenedor seccion relative flex flex-col gap-8 md:gap-12">
    <h2 class="seccion-titulo">{t(idioma, 'ediciones.laJornada')}</h2>
    {
      data.galeria.length > 0 ? (
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 md:grid md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-x-6 md:gap-y-0">
          {data.galeria.map((foto, indice) => (
            <div
              class={POSICIONES[indice % POSICIONES.length]}
              style={`max-width: ${foto.image.width}px;`}
            >
              {/* `grid`, not `block`: this anchor is what actually contains
                  `.foto-pegada`, so it is the box that has to give the
                  inline-block a definite width (see POSICIONES above). Without
                  JavaScript it is a plain link to the file; `Lightbox.astro`
                  upgrades it through `data-galeria-foto` (SM-038). */}
              <a
                href={foto.image.src}
                class="grid focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-azul-sello"
                data-galeria-foto
                data-indice={String(indice)}
              >
                <FotoPegada
                  imagen={foto.image}
                  alt={foto.alt[idioma]}
                  rotacion={ROTACIONES[indice % ROTACIONES.length]}
                  widths={[480, 960, foto.image.width]}
                  sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 88vw"
                />
              </a>
              {foto.credito !== undefined && (
                <p class="font-mono text-metadatos text-grafito m-0 mt-3">{foto.credito}</p>
              )}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <p class="text-grafito m-0 max-w-[65ch] font-mono text-base leading-relaxed text-pretty">
          {t(idioma, 'estados.fotosDelDia')}
        </p>
      )
    }
    {
      /* Vertical in the right margin on desktop, horizontal and centered at the
        end on mobile (Edicion.dc.html's NOTA PARA DESARROLLO). Only one of the
        two is ever in the accessibility tree: the other is `display: none`.
        Both wrappers state a width for the same reason the collage items do —
        `PalabrasClave`'s image branch sizes itself with `min(100%, …)`, which
        resolves to 0 inside a shrink-to-fit box. Each value is the component's
        own formula at that `tamano`: `calc(3rem * 3.2)` = 154px for the rotated
        vertical footprint, and that times the source's 376/281 ratio = 172px for
        the horizontal one at `2.5rem`. */
    }
    <div class="absolute top-4 right-0 hidden w-[154px] md:block">
      <PalabrasClave imagen={palabrasClaveImagen} orientacion="vertical" tamano="3rem" />
    </div>
    <div class="w-[172px] max-w-full self-center md:hidden">
      <PalabrasClave imagen={palabrasClaveImagen} tamano="2.5rem" />
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    /* CIERRE — sitemap.md §2.6 block 11, without the annotation the lamina does
      not have (see the OBSERVACIÓN in this file's header). */
  }
  <section class="contenedor seccion flex flex-col items-start pb-16 md:pb-24">
    <Boton href={rutaLocalizada('/apoyar', idioma)} variante="sello" anchoCompletoMobile>
      {t(idioma, 'botones.comoApoyar')}
    </Boton>
  </section>

  {
    fotosDelDia.length > 0 && (
      <Lightbox fotos={fotosDelDia} prefijoPie={etiquetaCorta} idioma={idioma} />
    )
  }
</Pagina>
